0018: GI server (real-time GI work packages R-03 and R-04). Client exports RemixBridge_GiOpen, RemixBridge_GiSubmit, RemixBridge_GiSolve, RemixBridge_GiPoll, RemixBridge_GiCancel and RemixBridge_GiReadCounters (client.giServer, default off). On the first open the server starts a worker thread with its own Vulkan device on DXVK's GPU (matched by deviceUUID through DXVK's interop interface; ray query and acceleration structures enabled when present, server.giMaxLevel). RemixBridge_GiSubmit sends a scene (triangles with a texel patch for each side, texels with their reflectance and target pixel) and a lamp table through two shared submit slots of 448 KB, in parts; the worker builds the ray structure or a grid and traces each texel's links once. A solve with a scene ticket computes one lamp's direct light and a fixed count of ray-free gathers (gi_solve.comp, one kernel for the ray-query and the compute level) in slices sized to server.giSliceUs (2000) of GPU time by GPU timestamps, and keeps the layers of lamps that did not change; a solve without one fills the prototype's pattern. The play thread copies finished results into the named DEFAULT-pool texture through a SYSTEMMEM staging texture and UpdateSurface, at Present and every 64 commands, at most server.giUploadBudgetKB (1024) a pass, a larger result in bands of rows, then publishes the ticket in a shared answer slot. Reset, ResetEx and device destroy answer open tickets D3DERR_DEVICELOST. Test: test-gi.cmd (test_gi_device). Needs Vulkan-Headers, volk and glslang in submodules\ (build.cmd fetches them).
Applies after 0001-0014 and 0017 on NVIDIAGameWorks/dxvk-remix f35b86a (bridge/ only); checked without 0015-0016.
diff --git a/bridge/bridge.conf b/bridge/bridge.conf
index ef9451ff23d8c097af3c973c50e777dcae0acf4e..97ded32da983cd3e2d62a95ff29f7911fa8c1228 100644
--- a/bridge/bridge.conf
+++ b/bridge/bridge.conf
@@ -138,6 +138,49 @@
 
 # client.asyncReadback = False
 
+#
+# Lets callers of the client exports RemixBridge_GiOpen, RemixBridge_GiSolve and RemixBridge_GiPoll
+# have a worker in the server, on its own Vulkan device, compute into a DEFAULT-pool texture they name.
+# RemixBridge_GiSubmit sends the scene and the lamps the worker solves. The server copies results in on
+# its command thread. Its GI block takes about 900 KB of the client's address space once
+# RemixBridge_GiOpen maps it.
+#
+# Supported values: True, False
+
+# client.giServer = False
+
+#
+# The server answers RemixBridge_GiOpen only while this is True. With False the client reports
+# the GI level none, as with a server without GI support.
+#
+# Supported values: True, False
+
+# server.giServer = True
+
+#
+# Bytes of GI results the server copies into textures in one pass, at Present and every 64 commands.
+# A result larger than the budget is copied in bands of rows over several passes.
+
+# server.giUploadBudgetKB = 1024
+
+#
+# GPU time of one slice of the GI worker's solve, in microseconds. The worker measures each slice
+# with GPU timestamps and sizes the next one to this budget.
+
+# server.giSliceUs = 2000
+
+#
+# Microseconds the GI worker waits between two slices, which leaves the GPU to the renderer.
+
+# server.giSliceIdleUs = 0
+
+#
+# The highest GI level the worker uses: 2 uses ray queries when the GPU has them, 1 stays on compute.
+#
+# Supported values: 1, 2
+
+# server.giMaxLevel = 2
+
 
 #
 # Server Settings
